{"raw": {"https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-Of-Career-Advising_JR101585": {"title": "Assistant Director Of Career Advising", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director reports to the Senior Associate Director of Career Education and supports the Center\u2019s mission to provide effective educational programs and services to advise diverse students and alumni with their career planning and professional development. Position Title: Assistant Director - Career Center Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time Supervisor: Senior Associate Director of Career Education Position Purpose: \u00a0 The Assistant Director reports to the Senior Associate Director of Career Education and supports the Center\u2019s mission to provide effective educational programs and services to advise diverse students and alumni with their career planning and professional development. Provide effective career advising through individual appointments with diverse students and alumni.\u00a0 Collaborate with members of the campus community to develop and implement career education programming. Engage alumni and students in career education programming.\u00a0 Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Career Advising :\u00a0Provides career advising to undergraduate students and alumni on all aspects of career planning, internship and employment/graduate school preparation. Provides individual and group instruction on various platforms and databases to be utilized by students for career exploration, networking, and internship/job search. Collaboration: \u00a0Works closely with employer relations team to support and promote employer and alumni engagement, consortia events, career fairs and other programming. Collaborates with on-campus constituents to provide career readiness and professional development opportunities for students across campus. Program Development and Training: \u00a0Designs, coordinates, and presents\u00a0career readiness workshops and programs that address the needs of students across all four years. Evaluates effectiveness of programs/resources/technology and reports career education outcomes.\u00a0 Administration: \u00a0Utilizes Handshake and Nexus platforms for student engagement management and supports content creation and management for UReady curriculum. Supervises career assistants to support assigned project work. Pitches in to assist colleagues as needed.\u00a0 Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus one to three years of direct 1:1 career advising experience, preferably in a private liberal arts higher education setting, and/or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and work experience. Demonstrated familiarity with the internship and employment recruitment process. Exceptional interpersonal, communication, presentation and teamwork skills to interact with varied constituencies (faculty, staff, students, alumni, parents, and employers). Strong attention to detail with the ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines. Exceptional judgment, ensure strict confidentiality, and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. Demonstrated ability to support, contribute to and strengthen a vibrant, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community of students, alumni, faculty, and fellow staff colleagues. Willingness to conduct presentations occasionally during evenings, weekends, and work some holidays. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in a related discipline. Experience with administration of career related assessments (e.g., MBTI, Clifton Strengths). Knowledge of college student development. Familiarity with career management platforms and educational technologies (e.g. Handshake, PeopleGrove, Nexus, LinkedIn). \u00a0 Desire to attend student-related events of interest outside of working hours. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $62,353.20. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Web-Designer---Digital-Strategist_JR101845": {"title": "Web Designer & Digital Strategist", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a versatile, energetic, and self-motivated Web Designer & Digital Strategist to take ownership of our web-based digital presence. As part of a small, nimble web team at Union, this is a unique \"soup-to-nuts\" opportunity for an entrepreneurial professional looking to make a direct impact. Web Designer & Digital Strategist Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Location: Hybrid available. \u00a0 Position Purpose: In this role, you will bridge visual web design, digital content strategy, and light front-end execution in a Drupal environment. If you thrive in a collaborative environment where everyone wears multiple hats and you crave the opportunity to help shape your role to meet organizational goals, this position is for you. \u00a0 You will work as part of a two-person web team reporting to the Vice President for Communications and Marketing, and working in close collaboration with the Assistant VP for Content Strategy. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: End-to-End Web & Visual Design: Conceptualize and design responsive web layouts, landing pages, digital campaign assets and user interfaces that align with the college's brand and admissions goals. Content Strategy & Digital Storytelling: Collaborate across departments to plan, structure, and refine digital content, ensuring site navigation, page architecture, and messaging effectively to students, faculty and alumni. Drupal Management & Light Front-End Work: Manage and update site layouts within our Drupal CMS, applying light CSS/HTML modifications and front-end tweaks to enhance user experience and maintain site aesthetics. Digital Brand Stewardship: Working with our CMO and AVP for Content Strategy, maintain and evolve digital visual standards, ensuring brand consistency across all public-facing digital channels. Cross-Departmental Collaboration: Serve as a strategic digital partner to internal campus stakeholders\u2014helping translate their departmental goals into effective web solutions. All-Hands Pitching In: As part of a small team, step in where needed to support team initiatives, web initiatives, and broader campus communications. \u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications: Experience: 4-6+ years of digital/web design experience, with flexibility for a high-energy candidate possessing strong entrepreneurial initiative and a broad skill set required. Visual & Web Design: Portfolio demonstrating clean web layout design, strong typography, intuitive UX/UI principles, and responsive design execution. Content Strategy Interest: Experience or strong interest in user journey mapping, content hierarchy, copy editing, and digital media strategy. CMS Experience: Hands-on experience working inside a Content Management System (Drupal experience is highly desirable). Technical Aptitude: Basic to intermediate front-end coding skills (HTML, CSS, basic JavaScript) to implement design tweaks and troubleshoot page layouts. Project Management skills: An ability to work collaboratively with clients to shepherd projects throughout the entire process. Adaptability & Initiative: Self-directed mindset with a desire to take ownership, solve diverse challenges, and shape a role in an \"all hands on deck\" higher education environment. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience in higher education or working with non-profit / institutional brands. Familiarity with web accessibility guidelines (WCAG) in an academic setting. Basic experience with digital analytics (Google Analytics) or SEO best practices to inform content strategy decisions. Bachelor\u2019s or other degree. \u00a0 Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $75,000 - $85,000. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-Of-Employer-Relations_JR101841": {"title": "Assistant Director Of Employer Relations", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nAssistant Director of Employer Relations Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time, In-Person. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Director - Becker Career Center Position Purpose: The Assistant Director of Employer Relations reports to the Career Center Director and supports employer engagement, campus recruiting, and signature career preparation programs at Union College. This role coordinates recruiting, oversees consortia involvement, and builds strategic career pipelines by connecting students with opportunities through employers and alumni. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: \u00a0 Campus Recruiting & Programming (85%) Conduct proactive outreach to organizations with a goal of establishing partnerships and opportunities for Union College students.\u00a0 Coordinates the campus recruiting cycles, and weekly event schedule of outreach tables, coffee chats, and information sessions on behalf of employers, graduate schools, and alumni.\u00a0 Support logistical details, communication and marketing of employer, alumni, networking, and consortium events, educational site visits, and annual on-campus career fair. Support Union Financial Network programming including preparatory and on-site events for UFN Bootcamp in New York City. Represent the college on the Capital Region Career Consortium (CRCC) for joint events and regional recruiting initiatives. Collaborates with Director to report outcomes assessing the effectiveness of employer relations\u2019 programs. \u00a0 Institutional Collaborations (15%) Collaborate with faculty to support student preparation and search strategies for experiential education courses and activities. Partner with College Relations to build and leverage alumni connections to engage in networking, mentoring and recruiting opportunities for students Manage the Union College alumni networking platform including communications and marketing materials for both students and alumni users. \u00a0 Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required; or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience will be considered. Familiarity with career services, corporate recruiting, or higher education relationship management desired. Familiarity with Handshake and client relationship management software desired. Strong interpersonal, communication and relationship-building skills to navigate both external and college-wide partnerships. Strong strategic thinking, program evaluation, project and time management skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends as required. Compensation: The annual salary rate for this position is $62,353.20. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Director-Of-Environmental-Health---Safety_JR101838": {"title": "Director of Environmental Health & Safety", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nDirector of Environmental Health & Safety (EHS) \u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. \u00a0 Work Location: This position is an onsite role and is not eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Supervisor: Vice President for Human Resources and Chief of Staff. This position also collaborates closely and strategically with the Director of Campus Safety and the Director of Facilities as key institutional partners to align safety compliance with daily operations. Position Purpose: Manage the EHS Department staff and students employees. Oversee the College\u2019s radiation, laser, biosafety, chemical safety, fire safety, Occupational\u00a0 Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) and Campus Policies, and hazardous waste disposal programs. Ensure organizational compliance with local, state, and federal safety and environmental regulations, complete required periodic regulatory reports, and coordinate regulatory inspections. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Strategic Leadership, Governance & Program Management (30%) Develop and execute long- and short-range plans, policies, and operating procedures for the EHS department to build a proactive and collaborative culture of safety across campus. Hire, supervise, mentor, and evaluate EHS department staff. Partner with Union Finance to manage the EHS budget and forecast annual costs for services, supplies, etc. Chair the Academic Affairs Safety Committee and partner with faculty, staff, and administration to evaluate and continuously improve safety initiatives. Collaborate and partner with Facilities Services on code compliance and occupational health & safety within the departments including both large and small projects. Designs and delivers EHS safety training programs for students and employees. Stay current on EHS trends, innovations, and higher education safety benchmarks, introducing modern practices and systems. Work with Human Resources to recommend preventative safety measures and controls and investigate employee injury incidents. Regulatory Compliance, Audits & Agency Liaison (25%) Direct Union College\u2019s compliance with local, state, and federal health, safety, and environmental regulations (OSHA, EPA, NYSDEC, NYSDOH, NYS Office of Fire Prevention & Control, etc.). Monitor changing health, safety and environmental legislation, update institutional policies and practices accordingly. Lead the strategy, administration, and instructional delivery of institutional compliance and safety training programs (e.g., OSHA, Radiation Safety). Oversee mandatory compliance reporting and serve as the primary institutional liaison during official agency inspections and audits (NYS Cooling Tower Registries, Asbestos and lead safety reporting, and other facilities related reports). Academic, Laboratory & Specialized Safety Operations (20%) Responsible for oversight of Union\u2019s chemical inventory program (CEMS), safety training for authorized entry to the ISEC chemical stockroom and serves as the Chemical Hygiene Officer (CHO) for the College. Serve as the designated Biosafety Officer (BSO), Radiation Safety Officer (RSO) and Laser Safety Officer (LSO). Maintain compliance with Union\u2019s Radioactive Materials License conditions, and biosafety and laser safety standards, and inventory controls. Direct safety inspections, hazard assessments, and chemical hygiene programs in Science & Engineering research and teaching laboratories. Environmental Protection, Hazardous Materials & Bulk Storage (15%) Oversee environmental stewardship programs, including the Petroleum Bulk Storage (PBS) program and hazardous chemical/waste management. Direct hazmat spill response readiness, ensuring proper containment protocols, reporting, and maintenance of emergency spill equipment. Manage electronic and universal waste recycling programs. Fire Safety, Life Safety & Emergency Response (10%) Manage fire safety and life safety inspection and training schedules across academic, administrative, and residential physical environments. Serve as a campus community liaison and share relevant health and safety information. Respond to campus EHS emergencies, serving as the technical advisor during hazardous materials incidents or severe laboratory events. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree (in Occupational Health & Safety, Environmental Science, Engineering, Chemistry, or a related field) required. 6+ years of directly related experience in environmental health and safety leadership, preferably in higher education. Safety certifications preferred such as Certified Safety Professional (CSP), Certified Chemical Hygiene Officer (CCHO), Certified Hazardous Material Manager (CHMM), OSHA 10 or 30 hour general industry certification. Ability to lift 30 lbs. required. Thorough working knowledge of EPA, OSHA, NYSDEC, NYSDOL, NYSDOH, and NYS Office of Fire Prevention & Control regulations. Strong safety\u00a0 consciousness, communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Demonstrated capability to lead diverse teams, and ability to foster inclusive safety practices across campus. Able to anticipate, deliver on, and exceed the expectations of students, faculty, alumni, supervisees, and fellow staff colleagues, etc. Ability to respond to on-campus emergencies, inspect lab/workspace facilities, handle spill response equipment, and navigate campus buildings. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $95,000 - $110,000. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Cogeneration-Plant-Supervisor_JR101837": {"title": "Cogeneration Plant Supervisor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe Cogeneration Plant Supervisor is a key leader, mentor, and role model within the Union College Facilities Services Department. This position is central to ensuring the safe and environmentally compliant operation of the central plant. The working supervisor directly manages and actively participates with all operational and maintenance activities and oversees the downstream steam and chilled water distribution throughout the campus. Cogeneration Plant Supervisor Pay Status and Classification : Non-exempt, Regular full-time, In-person. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship.\u00a0 Supervisor : Assistant Director of Facilities Position Purpose: The Cogeneration Plant Supervisor is a key leader, mentor, and role model within the Union College Facilities Services Department. This position is central to ensuring the safe and environmentally compliant operation of the central plant. The working supervisor directly manages and actively participates with all operational and maintenance activities and oversees the downstream steam and chilled water distribution throughout the campus. The Supervisor oversees steam, chilled water, and power generation of the plant's operations, field utility distribution, while focusing on safety, efficiency, and team management. Their key responsibilities include: Team Leadership & Management: Guiding the staff who operate the plant's systems for generating power, heat, and cooling. This includes managing daily schedules, conducting regular team meetings, providing training, and performing annual performance reviews. Operational Oversight: Ensuring the plant is maintained in a clean and organized condition. Responsible for establishing and managing all operational data, logs, and reports required for both internal review and external environmental regulations. Communication & Development: Serving as the main point of contact for project updates and schedules. The Supervisor also provides ongoing training to their team to ensure their skills and knowledge of plant equipment are always up to date. Budgeting and Forecasting: Responsible for all aspects of the plant's budget, from preparation to ongoing management. This includes creating the plant's operating budget, as well as forecasting expenses for both routine operational needs and long-term deferred maintenance projects for both the plant and the campus. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Operations: Monitors plant performance metrics and operations to meet energy demands. Coordinate startup, shutdown, and emergency procedures for all plant systems. Assists in the creation, development, and review of standard operating procedures for plant equipment and ensures testing (water, cooling tower, etc) is compliant. Performs required water tests for boiler feed water and condensate and collaborates with vendors on the care and treatment of cooling towers. Assist in planning, implementing, and overseeing plant upgrades and system modifications. Operates 24/7 plant facility utilizing the gas compressor, turbine, Heat Recovery Steam Generator (HRSG), D-type steam boiler, absorption and centrifugal chillers, and cooling towers. Maintenance : Oversee preventive and corrective maintenance for a wide range of plant equipment including boilers, chillers, the HRSG, turbine, generators, cooling towers, and air compressors. Diagnoses problems and abnormal conditions (such as leaks or unusual noise) by utilizing resources, collecting data, and interpreting P&IDs to develop effective repair plans. Coordinates plant shutdowns and vendor services for key equipment, including the gas compressor, turbine, and chillers. Manages all maintenance tracking and scheduling using the work order system (Performo) . Environmental, Health, Safety, and Administration: Ensures Compliance: Manages all environmental and safety programs to guarantee the plant meets all federal, state, and local regulations. This includes monitoring air emissions, chemical controls, and all required permits. Promotes Safety: Leads the effort to maintain an accident-free workplace. The Supervisor sets the example for proper safety practices, including the use of protective gear and following procedures to prevent injury. Manages Emergencies: Is responsible for responding to all plant emergencies and ensuring the team follows the established response plan to protect people and property. Position may require working varied shifts including nights, weekends, and holiday coverage , as well as covering open shifts, as needed. Complies with department and college policies and procedures. Qualifications: Education: A Bachelor\u2019s degree (in Mechanical, Electrical, or related field) or Navy equivalent education and experience is required. Experience: 5-10+ years experience of operations and maintenance experience as a Plant Operator with relevant understanding of high-pressure steam boilers, steam generators, power generation equipment (turbines preferred), and utility distribution required.\u00a0 Experience with aligning, switching, isolating, and paralleling electrical equipment and systems utilizing 13.2kV and 480V is preferred. Skills: Knowledge of control systems and operating mechanical systems conforming to SOP\u2019s as developed for the plant.\u00a0 Good organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills are required.\u00a0 Computer skills, including MS Word, Excel, Adobe, Google Platform programs, Metasys (preferred), and Plant Control Systems for operation of physical plants preferred. Leadership:\u00a0 Provide staff with leadership and ensure accountability and safety are followed within college procedures as well as safety within the plant.\u00a0 Train, lead, and elevate staff to ensure safe operations of the plant.\u00a0 Availability: \u00a0 Ability to respond to on-campus emergencies, inspect, evaluate, and deploy staff and contractors for corrective measures. Licenses: \u00a0 Valid New York State Driver\u2019s license is required.\u00a0 License as a Stationary Engineer and/or valid Navy or plant operator is preferred. Compensation: The hourly range for this position is $38.00-$42.00. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-of-Gold-Alumni---Parent-Engagement_JR101840": {"title": "Assistant Director of Gold Alumni & Parent Engagement", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Alumni & Parent Alumni Engagement is responsible for developing and implementing strategies and programs that foster connection, participation, and affinity among current parents and families, graduates of the last decade (GOLD) alumni, and students transitioning to alumni status. Assistant Director - GOLD Alumni and Parent Engagement Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time, In-Person. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Work Location: This position is an onsite role and is not eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Supervisor: Director - Alumni & Parent Engagement Position Purpose: The Assistant Director of Alumni & Parent Alumni Engagement is responsible for developing and implementing strategies and programs that foster connection, participation, and affinity among current parents and families, graduates of the last decade (GOLD) alumni, and students transitioning to alumni status. Through strategic planning and execution of programs, communications, and engagement opportunities, this role helps create meaningful experiences for constituents that foster long-term relationships with the College. The Assistant Director manages parent and family engagement efforts, GOLD alumni and student-to-alumni transition programming, virtual and year-round engagement initiatives, and selected outreach activities that promote connection across key constituent groups. This role also supports assigned reunion committee engagement efforts and acts as a backup to the Associate Director during busy event periods, helping to enhance the overall capacity of the Alumni and Parent Engagement team during major planning and execution phases. A collaborative, relationship-focused professional, the Assistant Director works closely with campus partners, College Relations colleagues, faculty, staff, students, and volunteers to create welcoming, mission-aligned engagement opportunities. This role collaborates with Annual Giving and other College Relations teams to support long-term constituent loyalty and philanthropic engagement, while primarily responsible for developing engagement strategies rather than owning fundraising efforts. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Develop and implement a comprehensive parent and family engagement strategy that enhances relationships with the College and advances institutional priorities. Plan, execute, and assess programs and experiences for parents and families that promote connection, participation, and lasting affinity. Develop and oversee initiatives for GOLD alumni and student-to-alumni transitions that introduce emerging alumni to meaningful opportunities for lifelong engagement with the College. Manage virtual programs and other year-round engagement activities designed to reach parents, GOLD alumni, and other designated groups beyond major on-campus events. Create and support engagement opportunities that align with constituent interests and strengthen the bond between the College and its alumni and parent communities. Assist with reunion committee engagement efforts in collaboration with the Associate Director and the broader Alumni and Parent Engagement team, including volunteer communication, outreach, and enhancing the constituent experience. Provide backup support to the Associate Director during peak event times, including assistance with planning, staffing, communications, logistics, and follow-up for signature events and major weekends. Collaborate with campus partners, including Student Affairs, Admissions, academic departments, and other stakeholders, to develop programs that reflect and improve the student, parent, and GOLD alumni experience. Work with Advancement Communications and colleagues to craft and promote clear, effective messaging regarding parent, GOLD alumni, and year-round engagement initiatives. Partner with the Office of Annual Giving and other College Relations teams to support engagement strategies that foster long-term connections and philanthropic involvement, while maintaining the primary responsibility for solicitation strategy, donor goals, and fundraising performance with Annual Giving. Monitor participation, gather feedback, evaluate program outcomes, establish key performance metrics, and prepare reports to facilitate ongoing review and improvement. Encourage colleagues to ensure timely post-program follow-up, including attendance documentation, constituent coding, stewardship communication, and reporting. Contribute to a respectful, inclusive, and collaborative College community by demonstrating civil and respectful behavior with parents, alumni, faculty, staff, students, and visitors. Participate in and support various events and initiatives organized by the Office of Alumni and Parent Engagement, including occasional travel and work during evenings and weekends. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required; equivalent professional administrative experience will be considered. Minimum of 2\u20133 years of professional experience in alumni relations, advancement, higher education, volunteer management, event/program management, or a related field preferred. Demonstrated ability to develop and manage engagement programs and events from concept through execution and assessment. Experience recruiting, managing, motivating, and stewarding volunteers preferred. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively with alumni, volunteers, colleagues, campus partners, and other constituents. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously. Ability to exercise sound judgment, take initiative, solve problems independently, and work collaboratively as part of a team. Experience with databases, CRM systems, event-management platforms, email marketing tools, and Microsoft Office/Google Workspace preferred. Demonstrated commitment to creating welcoming and inclusive engagement opportunities for alumni from a wide range of backgrounds, generations, affinities, and geographic regions. Ability and willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends and travel as required for programs and events. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $62,000-$64,000. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Program-Assistant_JR101832": {"title": "Program Assistant", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nProvides administrative support to Alumni & Parent Engagement staff members. Serves as a collaborative team member to support and staff key events such as Homecoming, Family Weekend and ReUnion.\u00a0Provides operational support for regional alumni clubs and affinity programs.\u00a0Provides front-line support and excellent customer service to alumni and parents of the College. Program Assistant, Office of Alumni & Parent Engagement Work Days: Monday-Friday Shift Start/End Time: 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Hours Per Week : 40 Weeks Per Year : 52 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Regular Full Time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Work Location: This position is an onsite role and is not eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Position Purpose: Provides administrative support to Alumni & Parent Engagement staff members. Serves as a collaborative team member to support and staff key events such as Homecoming, Family Weekend and ReUnion.\u00a0Provides operational support for regional alumni clubs and affinity programs.\u00a0Provides front-line support and excellent customer service to alumni and parents of the College. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Customer Service : Provides outstanding customer service as the first point of contact for the Office of Alumni & Parent Engagement. Fields and troubleshoots requests while working closely with all offices within College Relations and the entire institution. Event Registration: Builds events using Anthology and manages the online registration process for major alumni events on campus (i.e. ReUnion, Homecoming and Family Weekend) and regional and affinity events. Pulls reports for invitation lists, log and track all event registrations, evaluate registrations for errors, process all payments, send confirmation emails, and follow up with registrants as warranted.\u00a0 Class Correspondents: Serves as the primary point of contact for class correspondents, who compile updates on their class for publication in the alumni magazine. APE Operations: Uses the online system to reconcile purchases for team members. Monitors department email accounts and phones to field inquiries from constituents. Enters contact reports and maintain accurate records. Prepares event materials for staff travel. General : Participates in developing and executing an annual strategic plan for the Office of Alumni & Parent Engagement. Staffs events as needed. Offers to pitch in to help colleagues during crunch times and overlapping deliverables. Qualifications: Associates degree and/or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience required. Strong oral and written communication skills, including attention to detail. Proficient in using a range of business office software applications and systems, including experience navigating a CRM and working knowledge of Microsoft Excel. Ability to quickly learn other software applications. Able to collaborate effectively with colleagues across the College to achieve shared goals and objectives. Able to exercise exceptional judgment, ensure strict confidentiality, and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. Able to work in a fast-paced environment and be self-motivated with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Able to support, contribute to, and strengthen a vibrant, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community of students, alumni, faculty, and fellow professionals. Strong oral and written communication skills, including attention to detail. Able to anticipate, deliver on, and exceed the expectations of alumni, students, guests, and colleagues. \u00a0 Preferred qualifications: Experience providing administrative support in a thriving business or non-profit organization, preferably a residential liberal arts college. Experience organizing and supporting events of a small and large scale. Ability to make recommendations to address issues as they arise. Comfortable learning and navigating new technology. Ability to work independently and multi-task. Experience working in higher education or non-profit management work. Compensation: The hourly rate for this position is $20.00. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-French_JR101805": {"title": "Assistant Professor of French", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-03\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for the position of tenure-track Assistant Professor in French and Francophone Studies, with a focus on Digital Humanities, beginning September 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by November 15, 2026 will receive priority consideration.\u00a0\u00a0 Position description: We seek a colleague with demonstrated excellence at all levels of language instruction (native or near-native fluency in French is required) and potential to teach upper-level Courses in French and/or translation courses that contribute to the College\u2019s Interdisciplinary Programs . Moreover, we seek a candidate with interest in leading our term abroad program to France. We are interested in teaching that makes use of linguistic and cultural materials related to multiple aspects of the French and Francophone worlds. Ph.D. must be in hand or near completion by 9/27. The successful candidate will be able to teach French classes at basic, intermediate, and advanced levels, as well as other courses in French and in English (thus open to the full campus community), will have experience in leading co-curricular programming (i.e., language tables, cultural events), and will offer courses that contribute to the College\u2019s Complex Questions curriculum . The successful candidate will furthermore exhibit promise for innovative, active scholarship with both broad and deep engagement with rigorous, creative research questions. Teaching load is 2 courses per 10-week trimester, 6 courses per academic year. \u00a0 About the Department of Modern Languages & Literatures: The selected candidate will join a vibrant and diverse department, with colleagues who value the community shared across our five language programs and seven language offerings. Department members are regularly recognized for their commitment to teaching and research, as evidenced by their scholarly production, innovative courses, and editorial activity, as well as by their distinction with internal and external awards of excellence. Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files. Only the materials listed below will be considered. \u00a0 Cover letter describing how your education, teaching and research, academic interests, and experience address the requirements of this position Curriculum vitae Teaching statement that outlines the goals and methods of your teaching, including information regarding strategies you\u2019ve developed for teaching students with academically and culturally diverse backgrounds Research statement that describes your past and recent scholarly activities, as well as the methods and principles that have governed those activities \u00a0 Please send questions and other inquiries to Michele Ricci Bell, Ph.D. at mllchair@union.edu. Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in teaching and research. \u00a0 Compensation The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Administrative-Coordinator_JR101828": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nProvides essential support to our Major Gifts, Principal Gifts, Planned Giving, Family Giving and Operations teams. Your strong database skills, meticulous attention to detail, and customer service focus will drive our success engaging alumni and friends of the College. Administrative Coordinator of Major Gifts Work Days: Monday-Friday Shift Start/End Time: 8:30 am-4:54 pm Hours Per Week : 37 Weeks Per Year : 52 \u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Regular full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. \u00a0 Work Location: This position is an onsite role and is not eligible for a hybrid work schedule. \u00a0 Supervisor: Director of Major Gifts Position Purpose: Provides essential support to our Major Gifts, Principal Gifts, Planned Giving, Family Giving and Operations teams. Your strong database skills, meticulous attention to detail, and customer service focus will drive our success engaging alumni and friends of the College. \u00a0 Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Donor Data & Database Management (Colleague / CASM) Donor Profile Maintenance: Update CRM donor records, including solicitation tracks, ratings, proposal types, cultivation plans, and fund allocations. Meeting Reports & Tracking: File meeting reports from Gift Officer meetings; extract meeting metrics and compile research requests from reports to email directly to key leadership. Stewardship: Run monthly planned giving society reports for gift officers to initiate personalized outreach; coordinates welcome letters, including letterhead printing, presidential signature routing, scanning, and CASM archiving. \u00a0 Financial & Budget Administration Expense Management: Prepare and submit Workday expense reports and mileage reimbursements for leadership and gift officers. Budget Tracking: Track, monitor, and run recurring budget reports. Procurement: Create Workday requisitions to purchase necessary office supplies. \u00a0 Office Operations & Administrative Support Calendar & Room Coordination: Manage calendar scheduling for Major Gifts team meetings and book meeting spaces on campus. Facilities & Inventory: Oversee office inventory, submit facilities maintenance requests, and update monthly office whiteboards. Mail & Logistics: Retrieve incoming mail and deliver for processing; generate and print envelope labels. Document Security: Ensure proper disposal of confidential donor materials via secure shredding protocols. \u00a0 Event Support Departmental Events: Assist in creating, planning, and executing events pertaining to Major Gifts and Planned Giving. Qualifications: Associate degree in Business Administration or a related field required; equivalent professional administrative experience will be considered. 2+ years of administrative support or project management support experience preferred. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, specifically Microsoft Excel (complex formulas, data analysis, and report generation) and Word mail merge capabilities. Strong working knowledge of Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Drive, Calendar). Experience with CRM administration, including custom report generation, database maintenance, and data integrity verification. Demonstrated ability to quickly learn and adopt new software platforms and business systems. Exceptional organizational and task-prioritization skills, with a proven track record of managing multiple competing demands in a fast-paced environment. Strong foundational project management skills, including deadline tracking and process oversight. Meticulous attention to detail and a high standard for data accuracy. Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across cross-functional teams. Compensation: The hourly rate for this position is $20.00. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Philosophy_JR101796": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for a full time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Philosophy, beginning September 1, 2027. The area of specialization is ethics and the area(s) of competence is open. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by December 1, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Position description: The ideal applicant will have a Ph.D. in philosophy by the start of the appointment. The successful applicant will be expected to teach in their area of expertise, offer courses in philosophy at the introductory and advanced levels, and contribute courses for Union's First-Year Inquiry and General Education programs. The teaching load is 2 courses per term with a one course reduction in the first year. Union College\u2019s academic year consists of three 10-week trimesters. \u00a0 About the Philosophy Department: The department hosts one of the most impressive Speaker Series of any undergraduate institution in the country and is also home to Ephemeris , an undergraduate philosophy journal, founded in 2001. The department also has a very active student-run philosophy club. The faculty have research interests in metaphysics, epistemology, ancient Greek philosophy, early modern philosophy, Latin American philosophy, feminist philosophy, aesthetics, social and political philosophy, Africana philosophy, and philosophy of mind. \u00a0 Union College also has a vibrant set of interdisciplinary programs, such as Law and Humanities, Gender, Sexuality and Women\u2019s Studies, and Environmental Policy, to name a few. The successful hire can develop courses in their area of expertise that may contribute to one or more of these interdisciplinary programs, a complete list of which may be found at: https://www.union.edu/interdisciplinary-studies. Applicants are invited to describe in their cover letter how they may contribute to interdisciplinary studies at the college. \u00a0 Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files. Only the materials listed below will be considered. \u00a0 Cover letter and a current CV (in a single pdf) Writing sample One sample syllabus in ethics Statement of research experience and interests Statement of teaching experience and philosophy \u00a0 Applicants invited to the first round of Zoom interviews will receive a request for the contact information of and letters from three professional references, at least one of whom can speak to the applicant's teaching experience. Please send questions and other inquiries to Krisanna Scheiter at scheitek@unionedu. Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in both research and teaching. \u00a0 Compensation The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500 .\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. \u00a0 Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director---Alumni-Engagement---Volunteer-Programs_JR101708": {"title": "Assistant Director - Alumni Engagement & Volunteer Programs", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement & Volunteer Programs is responsible for creating, executing, and maintaining programs and strategies that enhance alumni connection to the College through regional outreach, affinity groups, volunteer participation, and year-round opportunities for meaningful involvement Assistant Director - Alumni Engagement & Volunteer Programs Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time, In-Person. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Director - Alumni & Parent Engagement Position Purpose: The Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement & Volunteer Programs is responsible for creating, executing, and maintaining programs and strategies that enhance alumni connection to the College through regional outreach, affinity groups, volunteer participation, and year-round opportunities for meaningful involvement. Through thoughtful outreach, program development, and volunteer management, this role helps build lifelong relationships between alumni and the College, fosters community, and supports a culture of connection, service, and institutional pride. The Assistant Director collaborates with campus partners and College Relations colleagues to create opportunities that deepen alumni affinity and promote ongoing involvement with the College. This position provides leadership for regional and affinity engagement efforts, alumni volunteer recruitment and stewardship, and selected year-round alumni programs. The role also serves as a backup to the Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement for Alumni Council operations and volunteer continuity, helping to maintain strong communication, engagement, and follow-through across key volunteer structures. A collaborative and relationship-oriented professional, the Assistant Director must effectively manage multiple priorities, foster meaningful relationships with constituents, and turn engagement into lasting alumni connections. This role collaborates with Annual Giving and other College Relations colleagues to support broader institutional objectives, while Annual Giving maintains primary responsibility for solicitation strategies, reunion giving, volunteer fundraising efforts, and the annual fund performance. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Develop and execute a comprehensive alumni engagement plan for regional and affinity-based programs that enhances alumni connections to the College and aligns with institutional priorities. Plan, execute, and assess regional alumni events and affinity-based engagement activities to boost participation, build relationships, and create meaningful experiences for constituents. Recruit, onboard, train, support, and steward alumni volunteers in collaboration with the Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement and other College Relations team members. Develop and sustain effective volunteer engagement strategies, including setting clear expectations, establishing communication plans, implementing recognition efforts, and providing ongoing stewardship. Develop and oversee year-round alumni programs and initiatives that promote a sense of belonging, encourage participation, and support lifelong engagement beyond major signature weekends. Assist in the reunion committee engagement efforts alongside the Associate Director and the larger Alumni and Parent Engagement team, focusing on volunteer communication, participation, and the overall experience of constituents. Assist the Director with Alumni Council operations, volunteer continuity, and related communications as needed. Work with Advancement Communications and other campus partners to promote alumni engagement opportunities using clear, consistent, and audience-appropriate messaging. Collaborate with the Office of Annual Giving, Major Gifts, and other College Relations colleagues to identify highly engaged alumni and volunteers for deeper institutional involvement and philanthropic pipeline growth, while primarily focusing on engagement instead of fundraising strategy. Track engagement, volunteer efforts, and program results; develop metrics and generate reports to evaluate effectiveness and find areas for growth and improvement. Prompt appropriate colleagues to ensure timely follow-up on events and programs, including tracking attendance, coding constituents, stewardship communication, and internal reporting. Participate in and support other events and initiatives organized by the Office of Alumni and Parent Engagement, including occasional travel and work during evenings and weekends. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Minimum of 2\u20133 years of professional experience in alumni relations, advancement, higher education, volunteer management, event/program management, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to develop and manage engagement programs and events from concept through execution and assessment. Experience recruiting, managing, motivating, and stewarding volunteers preferred. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively with alumni, volunteers, colleagues, campus partners, and other constituents. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously. Ability to exercise sound judgment, take initiative, solve problems independently, and work collaboratively as part of a team. Experience with databases, CRM systems, event-management platforms, email marketing tools, and Microsoft Office/Google Workspace preferred. Demonstrated commitment to creating welcoming and inclusive engagement opportunities for alumni from a wide range of backgrounds, generations, affinities, and geographic regions. Ability and willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends and travel as required for programs and events. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $62,000-$64,000. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Anthropology_JR101768": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Anthropology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Anthropology, beginning September 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin on November 8, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by November 8 will receive priority consideration. Position description: We seek socio-cultural candidates whose research addresses, and who can teach courses on religion and gender and who could offer courses in some of the following areas: kinship, childhood, education, visual anthropology, and linguistic anthropology. Geographically, we are interested in areas underrepresented in the current Union College curriculum including Sub-Saharan Africa, the Caribbean, the Middle East, South Asia, Southeast Asia, East Asia, or among the indigenous peoples of the Americas or Oceania, but we will consider other areas not currently represented by faculty in the department. Ideally, the new faculty member would be willing to direct one of our ethnographic field schools in rotation with another faculty member. Candidates with a Ph.D. in Anthropology in hand and teaching experience are preferred, but ABD candidates, as well as candidates in closely related fields are welcome to apply. The successful candidate will teach six courses over three ten-week trimesters. About the Anthropology Department: The department prides itself on strong teaching, building relationships with students, and fostering a sense of community. Department members are active scholars who support each other\u2019s scholarship and who value the integration of research and teaching.\u00a0Anthropology at Union College contributes to many interdisciplinary programs and to the Complex Questions general education curriculum that focuses on global challenges and on social justice. The successful hire can develop courses in their area of expertise that may contribute to the college\u2019s general education curriculum as well as its interdisciplinary programs. We believe that creating and maintaining a welcoming and diverse environment is central to our department\u2019s mission. Department members actively seek ways of fostering an inclusive and supportive classroom environment both through internal department discussions and through attending workshops offered by the college. Further information may be found online at https://www.union.edu/anthropology Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as PDF files. Only the following materials will be considered: Cover letter CV Teaching statement Writing sample Sample syllabi (one or two). Send questions and other inquiries to Prof. Robert Samet at sametr@union.edu. Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in research and teaching.\u00a0 Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/General-Athletics-Assistant---Temporary_JR101808": {"title": "General Athletics Assistant - Temporary", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nPart time\n\nThe General Athletics Assistant - Temporary provides support for athletic event operations, facility management, game day administration, parking operations, and rental supervision. This position plays a key role in ensuring a positive experience for student-athletes, coaches, officials, spectators, and facility renters during athletic contests and special events. General Athletics Assistant - Temporary Work Days : Varied Shift Start/End Time: Varies based on the business need. Hours Per Week: 10 Weeks Per Year: Varies based on the business need. Pay status and classification : Non-exempt, Temporary part-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Director of Athletic Facilities & Event Management Position Purpose: The General Athletics Temporary Assistant provides support for athletic event operations, facility management, game day administration, parking operations, and rental supervision. This position plays a key role in ensuring a positive experience for student-athletes, coaches, officials, spectators, and facility renters during athletic contests and special events. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Assist with game day operations for varsity athletic contests, including setup, event support, and breakdown. Support parking operations during athletic events, managing traffic flow, directing guests, and maintaining safe access to facilities. Conduct facility opening and closing procedures as assigned. Assist with event setup and breakdown, including tables, chairs, signage, barricades, tents, and athletic equipment. Provide customer service and guidance to visiting teams, officials, spectators, and campus guests. Serve as on-site support during external facility rentals, ensuring compliance with facility policies and rental agreements. Monitor facilities during events and report maintenance, safety, or security concerns to supervisory staff. Assist with equipment transportation and storage. Support special events hosted by the Athletics Department and external organizations. Perform other operational and administrative duties as assigned. Qualifications: High school diploma required; college coursework or degree preferred. Interest in athletics, event management, sports administration, coaching, or facility operations. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Dependable, organized, and detail-oriented. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required by the athletics event schedule. Ability to lift and move equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in athletics, event operations, facility management, customer service, or parking operations. Familiarity with collegiate athletics and event environments. Working Conditions Primarily works in athletic venues and outdoor environments. Requires standing and walking for extended periods. Must be comfortable working in varying weather conditions and during large public events. Compensation: The hourly rate for this position is $20.00. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Financial-Services-Specialist-Accounts-Payable-Associate_JR101801": {"title": "Financial Services Specialist/Accounts Payable Associate", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nThe Financial Services Specialist/Accounts Payable Associate is responsible for Union College\u2019s corporate credit cards.\u00a0 This entails, but is not limited to, auditing expense reports, managing the timeliness in which expense reports are created and approved, ordering new cards, handling expired cards, and suspending cards. Financial Services Specialist/Accounts Payable Associate Work Days:\u00a0 Monday - Friday Shift Start/End Time:\u00a0 8AM-5PM Hours Per Week:\u00a0 40 Weeks Per Year:\u00a0 52 Pay Status and Classification: Non-Exempt, Regular full time, hybrid arrangement available. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Financial Services Manager/Bursar Position Purpose : The Financial Services Specialist/Accounts Payable Associate is responsible for Union College\u2019s corporate credit cards.\u00a0 This entails, but is not limited to, auditing expense reports, managing the timeliness in which expense reports are created and approved, ordering new cards, handling expired cards, and suspending cards. This position assists the Financial Services team with other tasks as necessary, including, supplier invoice audit, supplier invoice creation from purchase orders and supplier statement reconciliation. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Auditing expense reports Efficiently managing the creation and approval of expense reports Ordering new corporate credit cards as needed Dispositioning expired credit cards as needed Suspending credit cards as needed Auditing supplier invoices Creating supplier invoices Reconciling supplier statements Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 1-3 years of Accounts Payable experience required. A combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience will be considered. Experience with Corporate Card management preferred Attention to detail and accuracy Excellent organizational and time management skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills\u00a0 Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment Ability to prioritize tasks, manage workload efficiently and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Previous experience with the following systems/applications: Colleague, Workday, Microsoft Excel, Word, and Google Gmail Compensation: The hourly rate for this position is $21.50. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-English--Creative-Writing--Poetry-_JR101767": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English (Creative Writing: Poetry)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of English, beginning September 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by November 2, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Position description: The Department of English at Union College invites applications for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of English specializing in Poetry. Candidates must have an M.F.A. or Ph.D. in Creative Writing (Poetry) at the time of hire, experience in teaching creative writing, and an established publication record, such as a published book of poetry or the digital equivalent, or a series of poems published in peer-reviewed journals . Candidates will teach poetry workshops at all levels and literature electives of their own design; contribute to the college's Complex Questions general education curriculum; and develop a First-Year Inquiry course in line with their own interests. Preference will be given to candidates interested in organizing a departmental reading series. The teaching load is two classes per 10-week trimester for three trimesters per year (2-2-2). We are especially interested in candidates who work in digital poetics and/or digital studies more broadly, who incorporate digital tools and platforms into their teaching and/or their poetry publication, and who expand our digital course offerings, which may include contributions that cross with Computer Science, or programs in Digital Studies, Digital Media, and/or Science, Technology, and Society.\u00a0 In particular, we seek candidates with demonstrated interest and/or excellence in the creation, curation, and maintenance of a peer-reviewed online journal, magazine, or other digital resource for the publication and dissemination of undergraduate creative writing. Finally, we encourage applications from candidates who demonstrate through their teaching and service a commitment to underrepresented perspectives, including those of BIPOC and/or LGBTQIA+ writers. We welcome applications from candidates whose teaching could support Union\u2019s interdisciplinary programs in Africana Studies, American Studies, Asian Studies, Climate Change Studies, Environmental Studies, Film Studies, Gender, Sexuality & Women\u2019s Studies, Mental Health Care, Music Technology, Latin American and Caribbean Studies, Law & Humanities, Religious Studies, Russian & Eastern European Studies, and/or Public Health.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 About the English Department: The newcomer to our faculty will enter a spirited collective of academics, authors, and mentors. Within the Department of English at Union College, we foster a cooperative and encouraging environment dedicated to student achievement, offering a diverse array of pedagogical perspectives that bridge conventional and avant-garde explorations of letters and the craft of writing. We teach a broad range of courses that include introductions to various literary genres and those that confront the literary canon, as well as intermediate- and upper-level courses that consider traditional authors or time periods, in addition to thematic and/or theoretical approaches that examine literature\u2019s relationship to global challenges and social justice. This curriculum includes creative writing workshops in poetry, fiction, creative nonfiction, screenwriting, and more. Our courses help support the interdisciplinary programs listed above and others. In response to growing student interest, the English department launched a creative writing minor in Fall 2024, which continues to develop and which this poetry position directly supports. Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files. Only the materials listed below will be considered. Application letter Curriculum vitae Writing sample (up to 15 pages) Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages), which includes experiences, approaches, and classroom activities that increase inclusivity and community for students of various backgrounds and abilities. Please send questions and other inquiries to Bunkong Tuon, Chair of the Poetry Hiring Committee at tuonb@union.edu . Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in creative work, teaching, and departmental and institutional service.\u00a0 Compensation The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500. \u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Sculpture-and-3D-Design_JR101717": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Sculpture and 3D Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Visual Arts - Sculpture and 3D Design, beginning September 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by December 1 will receive priority consideration. Position description: The Department of Visual Arts at Union College seeks applications for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Sculpture and 3D Design, beginning September 1st, 2027. A completed MFA from an accredited institution, at least three years of teaching experience at the college level, and a successful record of creative scholarship are required. A strong record of exhibition and evidence of an active ongoing studio practice are essential. Teaching responsibilities consist of six in-person classes per year over three 10-week trimesters, including introductory Sculpture and 3D Design courses (required for the Visual Arts - Studio major), as well as advanced thematic or process-specific Sculpture courses depending on the candidate's field of specialty and department needs. We seek an artist-scholar who can teach traditional sculpture practice, including molding techniques in plaster, additive and subtractive techniques in wood and stone, introductory to advanced welding, and advanced mixed media techniques. The successful candidate will also demonstrate proficiency with digital fabrication tools and workflows, including software such as Rhino, Illustrator, and SolidWorks, as well as hands-on experience with CNC routers, laser cutters, and 3D printers. The department conceives this position as part of an evolution of the Sculpture curriculum to integrate these tools. In addition to contributing to the core Visual Arts curriculum, the intent of this position is to pursue and develop new opportunities for interdepartmental collaboration between the Visual Arts, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, and Civil and Environmental Engineering, with an intent to develop new interdisciplinary initiatives in fields like Digital Design, Industrial Design, or Architecture. The successful candidate will have the vision and experience to collaborate with Visual Arts department faculty and other departments to conceive, plan, and create such initiatives. Candidates should have a robust and promising exhibition record, with demonstrated potential for continued artistic success at the local, national, and international levels. The area of scholarly art practice is open, but we would especially welcome candidates with experience in fine art digital fabrication, industrial, or architectural design. In addition to the teaching load, the position includes departmental and collegewide service, academic advising, work with senior majors, honors thesis students, and advanced independent study students as necessary. The successful candidate will become part of a dynamic department that includes Studio Art (Digital Art, Drawing, Painting, Photography, Printmaking, and Sculpture) and Art History faculty. Additional responsibilities will include supervising a full-time Sculpture Studio technician and overseeing and working with the department chair on short and long-term planning of the Sculpture budget for equipment and materials. Faculty in the department also rotate the curatorial responsibilities for the Crowell and West Galleries in the Feigenbaum Center for Visual Arts, a two-space, 1000 sq. ft. gallery. Faculty are eligible to apply for funding to support their creative scholarly work, as well as for funding to enable new teaching initiatives. The Visual Arts Department supports a General Education curriculum with increased focus on Global Challenges and Social Justice in our Creative Arts and Design courses. Candidates who demonstrate engagement with contemporary issues and diverse perspectives in their scholarly work and/or in the classroom are especially encouraged to apply (see Gen Ed information on Union\u2019s website ). About the Visual Arts Department: Union\u2019s Visual Arts Department consists of four full-time faculty in Art History and five full-time faculty in Studio Art (Photography, Sculpture, Painting, Digital, and Printmaking). Our studio was gut renovated in 2016 and features state of the art equipment throughout our facilities, including three sculpture studios, with large format CNC router, four welding bays, a dedicated wood shop and separate 3D Design studio. Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files or as website links. Only the materials listed below will be considered. The deadline for submitting applications is December 1, 2026. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Please include: Include in a single pdf : Cover Letter, Artist Statement including a sketch of a future artistic trajectory and projects in development & Curriculum Vitae / Resume, including a list of courses taught as instructor of record with year and semester/term. Two syllabi from courses taught as instructor of record, saved in a single pdf A statement on teaching, which should include a discussion of teaching philosophy, teaching practice and experience, and a discussion of your approach to working with students from a wide range of artistic, academic, and personal backgrounds. Portfolio of recent professional work (20 images maximum, in one pdf or link to a website). Each image should include title, date, media, and dimensions. Examples of student work (20 images maximum, in one pdf or link to a website). Each image should include course name, date, and assignment. Please note that only 5 attachments are allowed per applicant so please consolidate the items in the first bullet. Please send questions and other inquiries to Laini Nemett at nemettl@union.edu . Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references.\u00a0 Compensation The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology---2-Positions_JR101718": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biology - 2 Positions", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for two tenure-track positions: one in Microbiology and the other in Immunology, beginning September 1, 2027. Applicants must have a PhD in the respective field. Post-doctoral or comparable professional work is desirable. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by October 1, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Position descriptions: We seek two biologists whose research addresses fundamental questions in, respectively, microbiology or immunology using cellular, molecular, and/or genetic approaches. We encourage all applicants with appropriate background and expertise to apply, particularly those candidates whose research investigates the cell/molecular mechanisms underlying microbial biology, immune function, or host-associated microbiome biology using modern and/or innovative experimental approaches ( e.g. , single-cell technologies, functional genomics, gene-editing, systems-level analyses, and/or bioinformatics techniques). Befitting the teacher-scholar model, our goal is to hire two outstanding colleagues with demonstrated commitments to both teaching and developing a successful research program that incorporates our students. Teaching responsibilities include an upper-level microbiology or immunology course with labs, contribution to the biology core curriculum at both the first and second-year level, and a course of their choice. About the Biology Department: The Department of Biological Sciences at Union College is committed to providing exceptional academic experiences and training for undergraduates seeking to understand what creates, sustains, and changes ourselves, other organisms, communities, and the environment. We contribute to numerous interdisciplinary programs including Biochemistry, Biomedical Engineering, Environmental Science and Policy, Environmental Engineering, Public Health, Nanotechnology, and Neuroscience\u00a0 ( https://www.union.edu/interdisciplinary-studies ). Housed in the newly-constructed Integrated Science and Engineering Complex, the Department is well equipped with modern instrumentation such as a microCT, multimodal microplate reader, confocal microscope, flow cytometer, cryostat, 3-D multi camera motion analysis system, Agilent Tapestation, Nanopore DNA sequencer, Qubit Fluorometer, RT-PCR instrument, scanning electron microscope, greenhouse space, growth chambers, and, sterile tissue culture and animal care facilities. We also have access to a continuous flow isotope mass spectrometer, elemental analyzer, and an ICPMS in Union College\u2019s Stable Isotope and Geochemistry Laboratory as well as analytical chemistry instrumentation including FLPC, HPLC, and LCMS through the Chemistry Department. The College is situated in close proximity to a variety of terrestrial and aquatic habitats in the Adirondack and Catskill Mountains, and the Mohawk watershed. We share Union College\u2019s commitment to lead with wisdom, empathy, and courage, particularly as it relates to creating a welcoming environment where every member of our community is respected and valued.\u00a0 We are committed to teaching and mentoring students, as well as supporting faculty, from a full range of backgrounds, perspectives, and identities. Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files. Only the materials listed below will be considered. Cover letter (please indicate which position you are applying for) CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Please send questions and other inquiries to Brian Cohen at MicroImmunosearch@union.edu. Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in either Microbiology or Immunology Compensation The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/IT-Finance-and-Procurement-Coordinator_JR101584": {"title": "IT Finance and Procurement Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nThe IT Finance and Procurement Coordinator is responsible for managing the full lifecycle of information technology assets and procurement activities, ensuring accurate tracking, fiscal responsibility, and compliance with institutional policies. This position oversees college-wide IT asset inventory, purchasing, and vendor coordination. Serving as the primary owner of IT procurement processes, the role provides guidance to faculty and staff on technology purchasing, manages vendor relationships and contracts, and maintains asset and purchasing records within TeamDynamix (TDX). IT Finance and Procurement Coordinator Pay Status and Classification: Non-Exempt, Regular Full-Time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Work Location: This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement.\u00a0 Supervisor: Chief Information Officer Essential Responsibilities and Duties: IT Procurement and Vendor Relationships Serves as the primary purchasing agent, managing quotes, purchasing, renewals, and coordination with vendors. Coordinates and fosters relationships with established vendors, fostering open communication and mutual accountability.\u00a0 Provides purchasing guidance to faculty and staff, helping ensure technology selections align with institutional standards, compatibility requirements, and budgetary guidelines. Handles ordering, tracking, and fulfillment of IT purchases and ensures timely and accurate processing of procurement activities. Asset and Software Lifecycle Management Maintains an accurate, up-to-date database for tracking all IT hardware and software assets across the campus.\u00a0 Handles, in collaboration with Client Services, the complete lifecycle of IT assets, including discovery, deployment, maintenance and compliant decommissioning/recycling. Coordinates software license management, ensuring adherence to vendor requirements and cost-effective subscription renewals.\u00a0 Oversees the receiving and check-in of vendor deliveries to ensure accuracy and proper documentation. Budgeting & Financial Oversight Collaborates with the CIO on annual budget development, multi-year financial planning and strategic forecasting.\u00a0 Monitors budget performance against actual spending, analyzing variances and providing regular reports to the CIO and ITS management team. Office Management In partnership with the CIO, organize office operations and procedures.\u00a0 Provide event support for ITS activities, including ordering food and any necessary supporting equipment.\u00a0 Maintain inventory of office supplies. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in a related field, or an Associate\u2019s degree combined with significant relevant professional experience in IT asset management, procurement, or technology operations. Proven experience managing IT hardware and software assets across the full lifecycle, including discovery, procurement, deployment, maintenance, and decommissioning. Demonstrated ability to manage vendor relationships, including pricing negotiations, order coordination, issue resolution, and ongoing communication. Experience maintaining procurement documentation, including purchase records, warranties, contracts, and renewal schedules, with strong attention to accuracy and audit readiness. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply institutional purchasing policies, budgetary guidelines, and compliance requirements. Proficiency with spreadsheet tools (e.g. Google Sheets, Excel) and familiarity with IT service management (ITSM) or asset management systems.\u00a0 TeamDynamix knowledge is a plus. Proven ability to contribute positively to a collaborative, team-oriented work environment that supports institutional priorities and service excellence. Strong organizational, analytical, and documentation skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with IT staff, vendors, and non-technical campus stakeholders. Ability to support, contribute to, and strengthen a diverse, inclusive, and collaborative campus community. Compensation: The expected rate for this position is $32.00-$34.00. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. NOTE: This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Club-Coach---Women-s-Club-Rugby_JR101739": {"title": "Club Coach - Women's Club Rugby", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nPart time\n\nCoaches, manages, and develops a competitive Club Rugby team (non-varsity, independent league member). Maintains and demonstrates a positive, collaborative spirit to work with the team, and a passion for the sport. Women\u2019s Club Rugby Coach Work Days: Varied Shift Start/End Time: Varies based on the business need.\u00a0 Hours Per Week: Varies based on the business need.\u00a0 Weeks Per Year: 15-20 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, temporary position.\u00a0 Supervisor: Director of Student Activities\u00a0 Position Purpose: Coaches, manages, and develops a competitive Club Rugby team (non-varsity, independent league member). Maintains and demonstrates a positive, collaborative spirit to work with the team, and a passion for the sport.\u00a0 Essential Responsibilities and Duties:\u00a0 Coaching: Demonstrates effective teaching methods and possesses excellent leadership. Designs coaching strategies and develops cohesive team mentality. Builds and maintains strong relationships with student athletes. Ensures the medical safety of all participants in collaboration with outside Athletic Trainers and Emergency Medical Services (EMS). Administration: Administers and plans, in collaboration with club student leaders, all aspects of the rugby program adhering to league and department compliance. Communicates injuries and reports incidents to the Student Activities department. Present at all on- and off-campus or league games during regular season(s), as well as daily practices (20 weeks total). Qualifications:\u00a0 Prior experience coaching and playing competitive rugby (preferably college-level) required. Current participation in recreational league (as coach or player) preferred.\u00a0 Current status as a compliant USA Rugby Certified Coach with minimum USA Rugby Intro to Coaching Certification or ability to obtain prior to the start of the season. Working knowledge of rugby league rules and regulations or willingness to obtain.\u00a0 Able to work a flexible schedule including evenings and weekends. Strong leadership and organizational skills. Ability to lift moderately heavy items (up to 30 lbs.) and stand, bend and stoop for extended periods of time. Able to support, contribute to, and strengthen a vibrant, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community of students, alumni, faculty, and fellow professionals. Ability to function independently, display strong attention to detail, work under pressure, and meet deadlines.\u00a0 Compensation: The expected rate for this position is $25.00 an hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-of-Financial-Aid_JR101709": {"title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Financial Aid at Union College supports the administration of the College\u2019s financial aid programs. Reporting to the Director of Financial Aid, the Assistant Director is responsible for the administration of assigned financial aid programs, policies, and procedures and for ensuring compliance with federal, state, and College regulations and statutes. The Assistant Director will administer assigned federal, state, and institutional aid programs; assist with the daily operations of the Office of Financial Aid; and provide counseling and support to students and families. Assistant Director of Financial Aid Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Work Location: This position is not eligible for a hybrid schedule. Supervisor: Director of Financial Aid Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Support the Director of Financial Aid in the administration of the College\u2019s comprehensive financial aid programs and services and contribute to the effective and efficient operation of the Office of Financial Aid. Administer assigned federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs in accordance with applicable federal and state regulations and Union College policies and procedures. Monitor programs for compliance and resolve conflicting information, discrepancies, and other issues affecting student eligibility or disbursement. Review prospective and currently enrolled student application materials and supporting documentation to determine eligibility for financial aid and accurately award assistance based on federal, state, and College eligibility policies. Counsel students and families in all aspects of financial aid and educational financing. Interpret federal rules and regulations and provide clear, accurate, and personalized guidance regarding financial aid eligibility, policies, procedures, and financing options. Maintain accurate and complete financial aid records and documentation in accordance with applicable federal, state, and College requirements. Collaborate with Admissions, Bursar, Registrar, academic departments, and other campus offices to ensure effective coordination of financial aid processes, accurate information, and seamless student service. Qualifications: Required: Bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet established deadlines, maintain accurate records, and work effectively both independently and collaboratively. Experience learning and becoming proficient with a variety of computer applications. Preferred: Experience in financial aid or higher education enrollment management or student services. Familiarity with the Ellucian Colleague financial aid or similar student information system and financial aid administration software. Compensation: The annual salary rate for this position is $62,353.20 .\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Custodian---PT_JR101680": {"title": "Custodian - PT", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nCustodians are responsible for maintaining the cleanliness of office spaces and common spaces across campus. Custodian - Part time Work Days: Monday through Friday Shift Start/End Time : 5:00 a.m. - 10:00 a.m. Hours Per Week: 25 Weeks Per Year: 52 \u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt. Regular, Part-time. \u00a0 Supervisor: Team Lead Position Purpose: Responsible for trash removal and maintaining the cleanliness of office spaces and common spaces across campus. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Cleaning and Maintenance: Removes office and building trash. Washes windows, cleans showers, bathrooms, and public areas using wet/dry mop, vacuum cleaner, cleaning cloths and cleaning solutions. Follows safety instructions/procedures related to clothing, gloves, goggles, masks and use of cleaning chemicals. Cleans, strips and waxes tile and floors. Shampoos and extracts carpeting. Maintains vacuums and other equipment by making simple adjustments such as installing new vacuum bags and mop heads, moving equipment from location to location as necessary. Removes snow from entryways and walkways. Event Preparation Assistance: Assists with special events including but not limited to table and chair setup. Additional Tasks: Pitches in to assist colleagues when needed. Qualifications: Physical requirements: Ability to lift moderately heavy items (up to 50 lbs.), and stand, bend and stoop for extended periods of time. Must be safety conscious, able to read, write and understand written and verbal instructions and work with a diverse group of staff and students. Ability to work on weekends may be required. During emergency situations will be required to work in the event of a personnel shortage. Must have a valid driver's license with a clean driving record for cleaning jobs that include weekends. Does not apply to part-time cleaning jobs. The ability to foster and enhance a thriving, diverse, inclusive, and culturally vibrant community, while promoting a sense of belonging among students, faculty and staff colleagues, and alumni. Ability to read, write and understand written and verbal instructions. Compensation: The rate for this position is $16.00 an hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Developmental-Psychology_JR101687": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nUnion College invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of DEVELOPMENTAL PSYCHOLOGY, broadly defined, beginning September 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin on 9/1/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by 10/1/2026 will receive priority consideration. The Department of Psychology at Union College, Schenectady, New York, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor specializing in Developmental Psychology, broadly defined. The area of specialization is less important than research and teaching excellence. The ability to teach, advise, and mentor a diverse population of undergraduates is essential. Demonstrated understanding of teaching and conducting research in a small liberal arts college setting is especially desirable. Our new colleague will offer 2 courses per trimester at a variety of levels, including a combination of some of the following: introductory psychology, statistics, developmental psychology, and an upper-level seminar in developmental psychology within the applicant\u2019s domain. Desirable research areas include, but are not limited to, cognitive, social, emotional, moral, or language development; developmental psychopathology; clinically relevant or neurodevelopmental approaches; cultural and contextual influences on development; and applied or translational research. We would be especially interested in scholars who study cultural differences, racial inequality, or under-resourced communities. We also welcome a colleague with the ability to provide a developmental perspective on topics that contribute to the College's general education curriculum . We expect that our new colleague will establish and maintain a dynamic research program that involves our undergraduate students. A PhD in Psychology or a related field by appointment date is required. The college and department provide outstanding research support, including generous startup funds, and ongoing internal funding opportunities for both faculty and student research. Nearby schools, children\u2019s museums, childcare facilities, and farmers\u2019 markets offer participant-recruitment opportunities. Shared departmental resources include eye-tracking and electroencephalography (EEG) equipment. The college also maintains an active Faculty Development Institute that provides mentorship and various other forms of support towards growing faculty teaching, scholarship, and leadership. About the Psychology Department: The Psychology department consists of 13 accomplished scholars at various career stages, with diverse research expertise. We teach small courses and work closely with students, who are active in our research laboratories. We have ample research facilities, institutional support for student research, and host a vibrant speaker series that supports research collaborations. The department recognizes the rich possibilities of interdisciplinary studies and currently provides support for the Gender, Sexuality, and Women\u2019s Studies and Neuroscience programs. The department is strongly committed to creating and maintaining a welcoming environment for individuals from a full range of backgrounds,\u00a0perspectives, and identities, which is central to developing a rigorous and informed education in Psychology, and to our mission of preparing students for a globally interconnected world. Our goal is to create and support a diverse environment in which people from varied backgrounds can succeed and thrive. The College is located in New York\u2019s Capital Region, a metropolitan area of over one million people. Our region offers affordable, livable neighborhoods and a variety of interesting cultural and recreational opportunities. In addition, both New York City, Boston, and Montreal are located within a three-hour drive from campus. Application instructions: Please submit all application materials as pdf files. Only the materials listed below will be considered. Application letter Curriculum vitae Statements of teaching and research interests, which should include descriptions of experience, commitment, and activities toward making classroom and research spaces inclusive for all students, and/or how personal approaches to teaching and research can contribute to a diverse community Representative examples of 2-5 syllabi from courses you have taught (no course evaluations, please) Evidence of scholarship, including a representative selection of 2-5 peer-reviewed publications. Please direct inquiries to Joshua Hart, Chair of the search committee, at hartj@union.edu. Applicants invited to the first round of interviews will receive a request for the contact information for three professional references who can speak to their abilities in research, teaching, and departmental and institutional service. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $81,500-$83,500.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We offer exceptional benefits including: Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/College-Librarian-and-Director-of-Schaffer-Library_JR101681": {"title": "College Librarian and Director of Schaffer Library", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\nFull time\n\nUnion College seeks an innovative and collaborative leader to serve as the College Librarian and Director of Schaffer Library. Reporting to the Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of the Faculty, the Director leads a dedicated team of user-focused professional librarians and staff across Research & Engagement, Content & Digital Library Systems, and Special Collections and Archives and provides strategic direction and operational stewardship to ensure that Schaffer Library fully advances Union College\u2019s educational and scholarly mission in service of our students. The ideal candidate will combine a deep appreciation for the liberal arts tradition with the ability to collaboratively develop a forward-looking vision for how technology, data, and emerging generative AI tools can enhance undergraduate teaching, interdisciplinary research, and student learning. College Librarian and Director of Schaffer Library Pay Status and Classification: \u00a0 Exempt, Regular, Full-time. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. \u00a0 Work Location: This position is not eligible for a hybrid schedule. This position is eligible for relocation assistance. Supervisor: Vice President of Academic Affairs & Dean of the Faculty Position Purpose: Founded in 1795 as the first chartered college in New York State, Union College is a highly selective, independent liberal arts college committed to integrating arts, humanities, social sciences, science, and engineering. Schaffer Library sits at the heart of campus, providing crucial teaching and research support, a vibrant learning commons, and a core collection enhanced by Special Collections & Archives, a Permanent Collection of works of art, and the Adirondack Research Library.\u00a0 Union College seeks an innovative and collaborative leader to serve as the College Librarian and Director of Schaffer Library. Reporting to the Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of the Faculty, the Director leads a dedicated team of user-focused professional librarians and staff across Research & Engagement, Content & Digital Library Systems, and Special Collections and Archives and provides strategic direction and operational stewardship to ensure that Schaffer Library fully advances Union College\u2019s educational and scholarly mission in service of our students. The ideal candidate will combine a deep appreciation for the liberal arts tradition with the ability to collaboratively develop a forward-looking vision for how technology, data, and emerging generative AI tools can enhance undergraduate teaching, interdisciplinary research, and student learning. Essential Responsibilities and Duties\u00a0 Define, articulate, and advocate for a compelling vision for Schaffer Library aligned with Union\u2019s next strategic plan. Lead long-range planning and operational strategies, staying abreast of trends and innovations across small liberal arts college environments with regard to the ways in which libraries can enhance the student experience. Formulate, implement, and oversee the library budget. Leverage consortial and other opportunities to shepherd resources optimally, including identification of external funding opportunities. Recruit, supervise, mentor, and evaluate direct reports. Promote the professional growth of library faculty and oversee promotion applications, professional development leaves and other library personnel issues. Cultivate a user-focused, collaborative work environment across all library employees and promote diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in hiring, staffing, and public-facing services. Monitor curricular changes to ensure robust library support for academic programs. Oversee core library functions to help meet the teaching and research needs of students and faculty and records management needs of the college. Direct physical space planning to meet student needs and the preservation of library collections.\u00a0 Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA-accredited program. 5\u20137 years of progressive administrative and leadership experience in an academic library setting. Demonstrated record of success in budget management and personnel development. Proven leadership in supervising and supporting staff within a diverse, multicultural environment. Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, analytical, and collaborative problem-solving skills. Demonstrated track record of innovation, including the integration of emerging library technologies, e-resources, digital curation, and scholarly publishing. Ability to guide the College\u2019s integration of generative AI into its operations consistent with our values and goals. Familiarity with or proficiency in core academic library applications, systems, and technical platforms. Working knowledge of legal regulations and policies relevant to academic and research libraries, including copyright. Demonstrated commitment to fostering an inclusive, equitable working and learning community and promoting a sense of belonging across students, faculty, and staff. \u00a0 Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $170,000 to $177,000. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Men-s---Women-s-Cross-Country-Track---Field-Coach_JR101679": {"title": "Assistant Men's & Women's Cross Country/Track & Field Coach", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nResponsible for assisting in the organization, development, and leadership of a highly competitive Division III Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Cross Country/Track & Field program in support of the mission and core values of Union College. The Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Cross Country/Track & Field program is a member of NCAA Division III and the Liberty League. Union College sponsors 27 intercollegiate sports, 25 in Division III, with Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Ice Hockey competing at Division I. Assistant Men\u2019s & Women\u2019s Cross Country/Track & Field Coach Pay status and classification: Exempt, regular full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisors: Head Cross Country/Track & Field Coach Position Purpose: Responsible for assisting in the organization, development, and leadership of a highly competitive Division III Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Cross Country/Track & Field program in support of the mission and core values of Union College. The Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Cross Country/Track & Field program is a member of NCAA Division III and the Liberty League. Union College sponsors 27 intercollegiate sports, 25 in Division III, with Men\u2019s and Women\u2019s Ice Hockey competing at Division I. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Recruitment: \u00a0Assists in recruiting and retaining top prospective student athletes who are fully engaged in the mission of Union College. Collaborates with the head coach and admissions department to arrange on-campus visits for all prospective student-athletes and their families. Ensures compliance with all recruitment policies and procedures. Coaching: Demonstrates effective teaching methods and possesses excellent leadership. Travels to meets and competitions on the weekends. Student-Athlete Development: Works proactively with campus stakeholders to ensure the academic success of student-athletes. Mentors student-athletes. Administration: Supports aspects designated by the head coach of the program adhering to NCAA, league, and department compliance.\u00a0 Pitches in to assist colleagues as needed. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required, collegiate running/coaching experience preferred. Ability to work a flexible schedule including evenings and weekends. Must have an understanding of NCAA rules and regulations. Coaching philosophy compatible with a liberal arts college that upholds highly selective academic standards. Strong organizational, interpersonal, communication and computer skills needed. Ability to recruit within College, NCAA and Liberty League rules. Must be able to work with a diverse group of individuals. Preferred Qualifications: Collegiate Coaching Experience. Playing/Coaching experience as a cross country and/or track and field athlete. Experience in either the distance, sprints, or horizontal jumps. Experience leading young adults Speed/Power experience a plus Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $50,000-52,500 annually. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director--Student---Young-Alumni-Giving_JR101672": {"title": "Assistant Director, Student & Young Alumni Giving", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Student & Young Alumni Philanthropy leads the strategic development and execution of programs designed to build a culture of giving among students and recent graduates. This role directs the GOLD (Graduates of the Last Decade) program, manages student philanthropy initiatives, and oversees the Annual Giving Phonathon program, directly contributing to the College\u2019s engagement and fundraising goals. Position Title: Assistant Director, Student and Young Alumni Giving Pay Status and Classification: Exempt, Regular Full-time. This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Director of Annual Giving Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Young Alumni Philanthropy: Program Management: Lead and champion the GOLD program, driving a volunteer-led fundraising strategy for young alumni. Collaborate with Alumni & Parent Engagement to align philanthropic initiatives with broader engagement goals. Volunteer Management: Oversee the GOLD Committee to develop initiatives that increase young alumni participation. Lead fundraising efforts for 1st, 5th, and 10th ReUnion Committees. Portfolio Management: Cultivate and steward a portfolio of GOLD leadership donors and prospects, strategically advancing relationships to identify major gift potential. Student Philanthropy:\u00a0 Program Management: Expand student philanthropy program, including the senior class gift campaign, to educate students on the impact of giving Volunteer Management: Recruit and lead the Senior Class Gift Committee to champion the class campaign. Phonathon:\u00a0 Program Management: Oversee a dynamic Phonathon program that integrates with the Annual Giving solicitation strategy. Analyze performance data and prepare statistical reports for the Director of Annual Giving to refine program efficacy. Student Supervision: Recruit, train, and mentor student workers, fostering a positive, inclusive, and high-performance environment that motivates student callers to achieve fundraising goals \u200b General College Relations:\u00a0 Participates in the development and execution of an annual strategic plan for the Office of Annual Giving.\u00a0 Staff College Relations events as needed, including Homecoming and Family Weekend and ReUnion. Contribute to other campus initiatives and key college priorities if and when opportunities arise. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two or more years of experience in annual giving, development, alumni relations, or related fields, or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience.\u00a0 Strong understanding of philanthropy trends and best practices in higher education fundraising. Experience in managing and motivating student workers or volunteers. Demonstrated experience in developing and implementing successful fundraising strategies for students and young alumni. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. Ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders and foster an inclusive environment among students, alumni, and colleagues.\u00a0 Proficiency in data analysis and utilizing metrics to inform decision-making. Familiarity with fundraising software and Constituent Relationship Management (CRM) systems. Ability and willingness to travel, work occasional weekends, and participate in evening events as required.\u00a0 Passion for higher education and the mission of the College. Ability to exercise exceptional judgment, ensure strict confidentiality, and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. Compensation: The annual salary range for this position is $64,000.\u00a0 Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Licensed-Electrician_JR101601": {"title": "Licensed Electrician", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-17\nFull time\n\nPosition Purpose: The candidate will perform journey level quality work, and is responsible for the installation, maintenance, and repair of all college owned electrical systems and equipment. Licensed Electrician Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Regular full-time, In-Person; This position is not eligible for relocation assistance or visa sponsorship. Supervisor: Electrical Supervisor Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Operations: Meets the electrical needs of the campus community by performing work requests, emergencies, and special set-ups for faculty, staff and students. Works with various departments in order to achieve common goals and desires. Duties include: Ballast/driver, Switch/receptacle, and Breaker/Feeder replacements. Maintenance: Performs and maintains functionality of equipment and systems, including: Emergency Lighting, Switchgear, Variable Frequency Drives, Motor Control Centers, Transformers, and Battery back-up systems. Conducts monthly preventive maintenance in order to minimize equipment downtime. Projects: Plans and lays out work accordingly with knowledge and understanding of reading blue prints. Collaborates with team members on finding the best approach while leading to set an example. Lighting retrofits, additional circuitry, EV Charger installations, and feeder upgrades are some of the in-house team projects. Trouble-Shooting: Identifying and finding solutions when circumstances arise in order to maintain a 24/7 power generating facility. Ability to read and interpret one-line diagrams, diagnosis motor and motor control failures, and capacity to grow and develop skills through hands on training Qualifications: High school diploma, two-year technical trade school, or apprenticeship program, and/or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, and/or work experience. Five years as a Journeyman Electrician, experience in residential, commercial, and industrial applications.\u00a0 Valid Commercial Electrician\u2019s License (Preferred in Schenectady, Albany, or Troy). Must have good communication and interpersonal skills. Computer skills including (Word, Excel, and Adobe). Knowledge of medium voltage three phase systems (13.2KV), WYE/DELTA and low voltage systems (24, 120, 208, 277, and 480v).\u00a0 Available for round-the-clock emergency response both on and off campus. Strong understanding and application of the National Electrical Code, NFPA, and OSHA standards on electrical and work safety procedures. Compensation: The hourly range for this position is $31.00-33.00 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare: Medical (PPO & HDHP), Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition Exchange Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/On-Call-Officer_JR100175": {"title": "On-Call Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-11\nPart time\n\nPatrols buildings and grounds, responds to emergencies and performs related duties designed to promote and ensure a safe and secure campus environment. Work Days: Varies - On-Call Shift Start/End Time: Varies Hours Per Week : Varies\u00a0 Weeks Per Year: Varies Campus Safety Officer On-Call\u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Temporary Supervisor: First Sergeant Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Safety and Security Patrol: Patrols campus premises on foot or vehicle to ensure the safety and security of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Identifies and responds to potential security threats, suspicious activities, and safety hazards. Monitors access to campus buildings and facilities and ensures that only authorized individuals enter restricted areas. Directs traffic during peak hours, special events, or emergencies, ensuring smooth flow and pedestrian safety.\u00a0 Emergency Response: Responds promptly to emergency calls, provides first aid or assistance as needed, and coordinates with other emergency responders when required. Crime Prevention: Monitors access points, enforces campus policies, and addresses violations like trespassing, vandalism, and theft. Conducts security checks on buildings and facilities. Investigations: Collects evidence, interviews witnesses, and files detailed reports for further action by campus authorities or law enforcement if necessary. Safety Training and Awareness: Attends safety workshops, training sessions, and awareness programs related to personal safety, fire safety, and active shooter preparedness. Communication: Maintains clear and constant communication with other Campus Safety members, campus staff, and local law enforcement to coordinate responses to incidents effectively. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of experience in a related field, and/or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, or work experience. Associate\u2019s degree in a related field of study may be substituted for work experience.\u00a0 Valid NYS drivers license.\u00a0 Current New York State Security Guard registration certification required.\u00a0 Physical requirements: Ability to lift 50 lbs, walk and stand for extended periods, and climbing of stairs.\u00a0 Ability to work a flexible schedule, including weekends and evenings. Demonstrated conscientiousness related to safety and ability to follow procedures. Ability to exercise exceptional judgment, ensure strict confidentiality, and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. The ability to foster and enhance a thriving, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community, while promoting a sense of belonging among students, alumni, faculty, and staff colleagues. Able to anticipate, deliver on, and exceed the expectations of constituencies served e.g., students, faculty, alumni, colleagues and other community members.\u00a0 Able to proactively identify and pursue relevant learning and professional development opportunities and apply new knowledge, insights, and skills to enhance results. We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. Compensation: The rate for this position is $20.00 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Custodian---Temporary_JR100287": {"title": "Custodian - Temporary", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-10\nFull time\n\nResponsible for maintaining the cleanliness of office spaces and common spaces across campus. Work Days: Monday through Friday, with weekend availability Shift Start/End Times : 5:00 a.m. - 9:00 a.m. or 5:00 a.m. - 1:30 p.m. Hours Per Week: Varies based on business need. Weeks Per Year: Varies based on business need. Custodian - Temporary Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Temporary \u00a0 Supervisor: Team Lead Position Purpose: Responsible for maintaining the cleanliness of office spaces and common spaces across campus. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Cleaning and Maintenance: Removes office and building trash. Washes windows, cleans showers, bathrooms, and public areas using wet/dry mop, vacuum cleaner, cleaning cloths and cleaning solutions. Follows safety instructions/procedures related to clothing, gloves, goggles, masks and use of cleaning chemicals. Cleans, strips and waxes tile and floors. Shampoos and extracts carpeting. Maintains vacuums and other equipment by making simple adjustments such as installing new vacuum bags and mop heads, moving equipment from location to location as necessary. Removes snow from entryways and walkways. Event Preparation Assistance: Assists with special events including but not limited to table and chair setup. Additional Tasks: Pitches in to assist colleagues when needed. Qualifications: Physical requirements: Ability to lift moderately heavy items (up to 50 lbs.), and stand, bend and stoop for extended periods of time. Must be safety conscious, able to read, write and understand written and verbal instructions and work with a diverse group of staff and students. Ability to work on weekends may be required. During emergency situations will be required to work in the event of a personnel shortage. A valid NYS driver's license is preferred, but not required for part-time and temporary employment. The ability to foster and enhance a thriving, diverse, inclusive, and culturally vibrant community, while promoting a sense of belonging among students, faculty and staff colleagues, and alumni. Ability to read, write and understand written and verbal instructions. Compensation: The rate for this position is $16.00 an hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/On-Call-Officer_JR101081": {"title": "On-Call Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-26\nPart time\n\nPatrols buildings and grounds, responds to emergencies and performs related duties designed to promote and ensure a safe and secure campus environment. Work Days: Varies - On-Call Shift Start/End Time: Varies Hours Per Week : Varies\u00a0 Weeks Per Year: Varies Campus Safety Officer On-Call\u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Temporary Supervisor: First Sergeant Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Safety and Security Patrol: Patrols campus premises on foot or vehicle to ensure the safety and security of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Identifies and responds to potential security threats, suspicious activities, and safety hazards. Monitors access to campus buildings and facilities and ensures that only authorized individuals enter restricted areas. Directs traffic during peak hours, special events, or emergencies, ensuring smooth flow and pedestrian safety.\u00a0 Emergency Response: Responds promptly to emergency calls, provides first aid or assistance as needed, and coordinates with other emergency responders when required. Crime Prevention: Monitors access points, enforces campus policies, and addresses violations like trespassing, vandalism, and theft. Conducts security checks on buildings and facilities. Investigations: Collects evidence, interviews witnesses, and files detailed reports for further action by campus authorities or law enforcement if necessary. Safety Training and Awareness: Attends safety workshops, training sessions, and awareness programs related to personal safety, fire safety, and active shooter preparedness. Communication: Maintains clear and constant communication with other Campus Safety members, campus staff, and local law enforcement to coordinate responses to incidents effectively. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of experience in a related field, and/or a combination of relevant education, training, certifications, or work experience. Associate\u2019s degree in a related field of study may be substituted for work experience.\u00a0 Valid NYS drivers license.\u00a0 Current New York State Security Guard registration certification required.\u00a0 Physical requirements: Ability to lift 50 lbs, walk and stand for extended periods, and climbing of stairs.\u00a0 Ability to work a flexible schedule, including weekends and evenings. Demonstrated conscientiousness related to safety and ability to follow procedures. Ability to exercise exceptional judgment, ensure strict confidentiality, and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. The ability to foster and enhance a thriving, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community, while promoting a sense of belonging among students, alumni, faculty, and staff colleagues. Able to anticipate, deliver on, and exceed the expectations of constituencies served e.g., students, faculty, alumni, colleagues and other community members.\u00a0 Able to proactively identify and pursue relevant learning and professional development opportunities and apply new knowledge, insights, and skills to enhance results. We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. Compensation: The rate for this position is $20.00 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Senior-Stationary-Engineer_JR101434": {"title": "Senior Stationary Engineer", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-15\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Stationary Engineer will operate, maintain, and repair the equipment within the central plant facility as well as the downstream steam and chilled water distribution. Equipment includes: A Gas Fired Turbine, Steam boilers, HRSG, Gas Compressor, Absorption Chiller, Cooling Towers, Pumps and motors. Position Title: Senior Stationary Engineer Pay Status and Classification: Non-exempt, Regular full-time Supervisor: Cogeneration Plant Supervisor Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Operations : \u00a0 Performs the startup, shutdown, and emergency procedures for plant systems including: Gas fired turbine, Gas compressor, HRSG, Gas fired boilers, Absorption chiller, Centrifugal chillers, and Cooling tower. Performs water tests as required for the supply and treatment of boiler feed water and condensate, as well as works with vendors to support care and treatment of cooling towers. Assists the supervisor in planning, implementing, and overseeing plant upgrades and system modifications. Operate and or adjust PRV steam valves depending upon consumption for Absorption Chiller and or main steam distribution. Monitors control room instrumentation and alarms in order to identify deficiencies and take corrective actions. Utilizes the building management systems (BMS) for effective performance and or deficiency measures. Performs building switchovers by draining AHU coils units or filling depending upon season. Maintenance : Performs preventive and corrective maintenance for plant equipment including boilers, chillers, HRSG, turbine, generators, cooling towers, and air compressors. Identifies leaks, noise, and abnormal conditions, and makes recommendations, and or repairs. Periodically blows down centrifugal chillers during operations, as well as maintains proper flow through barrels, which may include cleaning strainers. Maintains steam and chilled water manholes by checking ground water pumps and operations.\u00a0 Works with vendors for services including the gas compressor, turbine, and chillers. Utilize the work order system (Works) to track and schedule maintenance. Participates in the creation and development of standard operating procedures (SOP\u2019s). Repair: Identify problem areas through utilizing resources, collecting data, and understanding P&ID\u2019s. Repairs and or replaces condensate and sump pumps, as well as performs alignments. Makes necessary repairs to various campus steam traps. Performs proper Lock-out-Tag-out when working on equipment. Working Conditions : \u00a0 The work area includes Central Plant and all campus facilities. Position may require working varied shifts including nights, weekends, and holiday coverage. Covering open shifts, as needed. Maintains a safe work environment through job planning, housekeeping, as well as identifying corrective hazards. Complies with department and college policies and procedures. Qualifications: Education :\u00a0 Associates degree in plant utilities, electrical, or mechanical engineering. High School diploma. Relevant Military Training will be considered. \u00a0 \u200b Experience: \u00a0 Five years\u2019 experience as a boiler operator/nuclear, and or stationary engineer. Experience in operating high pressure steam boilers and distribution. Experience with central plant chiller systems and distributed chilled water Experience with the operations of switching 13.2KV and 480v breakers through a Load Management System (LMS) preferred. Skills : Must have good communication and interpersonal skills. Computer skills including (Word, Excel, and Adobe). Knowledge of distributive control systems (DCS). Licenses: \u00a0 Valid New York State driver\u2019s license. Licensed as a Stationary Engineer, and/or Navy plant operator. Compensation: The hourly range for this position is $32-35 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting.\u00a0 Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best staff and faculty colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer exceptional benefits including: Generous Vacation, Sick, and Personal Time Winter Recess Break in Addition to Paid Holidays (in accordance with policy) Healthcare, Dental, and Vision Insurance\u00a0(Flexible Spending and Dependent Care Accounts) Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and Discounts for On-Campus Wellness Programs Employee Scholarships toward Certifications, Seminars, Training and Professional Development Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Salary Continuation Program in the event of Disability Tuition programs Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Van-Driver---On-Call_JR100128": {"title": "Van Driver - On Call", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-23\nPart time\n\nProvides transportation of Union College students, staff and community members to and from College approved locations following safety protocols - No CDL required for this position. Work Days: \u00a0 Varies \u2013 On Call Shift Start/End Time: \u00a0 Varies \u2013 On Call Hours Per Week : Varies Weeks Per Year : Varies Van Driver - On Call\u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: \u00a0Temporary, Non-exempt, Part-time. Supervisor: \u00a0 Transportation Manager Position Purpose: \u00a0 Provides transportation of Union College students, staff and community members to and from College approved locations following safety protocols.\u00a0 Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Safety Compliance: \u00a0 Conducts pre-trip inspections of equipment before each designated route. Reports concerns regarding vehicle safety, road hazards, and safety for the community being served i.e. road hazards, sick or intoxicated students to the immediate supervisor from Campus Safety. Complies with random drug and alcohol testing requirements. Trip Management and Reporting: \u00a0 Provides trip information to the dispatcher before each trip. Maintains scheduled times and locations for the 'Trolley Service.' Reports all incidents, whether minor or major, to the immediate supervisor from Campus Safety.\u00a0 Qualifications: Two or more years of transportation driving experience.\u00a0 Valid NYS Driver\u2019s License with a clean driving record.\u00a0 Strong communication skills and ability to exercise exceptional judgment and demonstrate outstanding professionalism in a range of situations. Demonstrated commitment to following safety procedures.\u00a0 Physical requirements: Must be able to sit for extended periods while operating a vehicle. Ability to lift, carry, and move objects up to 25 pounds as needed. Ability to enter and exit the vehicle frequently and assist passengers as necessary. Able to foster and enhance a thriving, culturally diverse, and inclusive learning community, while promoting a sense of belonging among students, alumni, faculty, and staff colleagues. Able to anticipate, deliver on, and exceed the expectations of constituencies served e.g., students, faculty, alumni, supervises, and colleagues.\u00a0 Compensation The expected rate for this position is $18.50 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Trolley-Driver--On-Call-_JR100127": {"title": "Trolley Driver - On Call", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-14\nPart time\n\nProvides transportation of Union College students, staff and community members to and from College approved locations following safety protocols - CDL Required Work Days: \u00a0 Varies \u2013 On Call Shift Start/End Time: \u00a0 Varies \u2013 On Call Hours Per Week: \u00a0 Varies Weeks Per Year: \u00a0 Varies Trolley Driver - On Call\u00a0 Pay Status and Classification: \u00a0 Temporary, Non-Exempt, Part-time. Supervisor: \u00a0Transportation Manager Position Purpose: \u00a0 Provides transportation of Union College students, staff and community members to and from College approved locations following safety protocols Responsibilities: Duties of the driver include a pre-trip inspection of the equipment to be used during the designated route Provide the dispatcher with trip information prior to the start of each trip Maintain the scheduled times and locations as posted for the Trolley Service Report all concerns of vehicle safety, including concerns of safety for the community being served, i.e. road hazards, sick or intoxicated students to the immediate supervisor from Campus Safety\u00a0 Report any incidents whether they appear minor or major to the driver Qualifications: Drivers must possess and maintain a valid New State Commercial Driver's License, minimum class \"B\" with \"P\" endorsement.\u00a0 2+ years of transportation driving experience Strong communications skills for working with a diverse group of college Faculty, Staff and Students. Drivers are subject to commercial driver\u2019s license (CDL) standards. All drivers are subject to random drug and alcohol testing as mandated by citations \u201c49 CFR 382\u201d & \u201c49 CFR 40\u201d Physical requirements: Must be able to sit for extended periods while operating a vehicle. Ability to lift, carry, and move objects up to 25 pounds as needed. Ability to enter and exit the vehicle frequently and assist passengers as necessary. Compensation: The expected rate for this position is $19.00 per hour. Except for roles with a set rate of pay, the wage/salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The stated hiring rate/range represents the College\u2019s good faith and reasonable estimate of the rate/range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Location: Schenectady, NY We know some job seekers may not apply for career opportunities unless they meet every qualification in the position description including the preferred qualifications. We are most interested in hiring the best colleagues, and recognize that a successful candidate may come from a less traditional career path. We encourage you to apply, even if you don\u2019t believe you meet every one of our preferred qualifications. We offer great benefits even for temporary employees, including: Free On-Campus Fitness Facility Access and On-Campus Wellness Programs Pre and Post Tax participation in a 403(b) Retirement Plan Background Checks: In accordance with our background check policy , finalists for hire will undergo a background check that includes education, employment, and criminal convictions. E-Verify Participation: \u00a0Union College participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States. Learn more about E-Verify and your Right to Work (Derecho a Trabajar) ."}}, "rows": {"https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-Of-Career-Advising_JR101585": {"school_id": 1005, "posting_url": "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-College-Schenectady-NY/Assistant-Director-Of-Career-Advising_JR101585", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Director Of Career Advising", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-19"}, "https://unioncollege.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UnionCollegeCareers/job/Union-Coll